    "overflowAndShell": "Wide current-page screenshots reach the real shared footer with sidebar/main edges aligned. Narrow screenshots show the natural stacked navigation and actual scrolling needed to reach the current page. Text is not horizontally clipped; page/step targets are fully in viewport. Captures focus on different scroll positions, not an assertion that all controls fit one viewport.",
    "priorF02UX01": "Earlier effective-child-margin, exact panel inventory, genuine short-shell, long-page, narrow stacking and keyboard/scroll findings remain closed by the retained preflight/test and visual history. Fresh six settings validators plus current source binding and selected current Task Center pixels show no incremental regression. This round did not repeat the dedicated short-shell fixture or the complete prior product suite.",
    "contextActions": "Previous visual02 F01 remains closed: current source retains the shared Button implementation, and wide current-step supplemental pixels again show coherent disabled Next and enabled Return controls. The unchanged recorder confirmed 2 context buttons, 1 enabled and 1 actually traversed in all 6 settings cases. No new claim that Previous is rendered in the first-step fixture is made.",
    "themeContrast": "All 30 direct rendered text samples meet normal-text AA without exemption: light label 8.0585755, light marker 5.1685556, light metadata 4.7049090; dark label 6.1923038, dark marker 5.0606172, dark metadata 7.1538378. Metadata and the aria-hidden visual number were included.",
    "authority": "No normative reference change is inferred. Semantic workflow identity 1.5 and unknown checkpoint authority remain visible and truthful under the approved presentation-1.6 overlay."
